storcli for loong64 / riscv64
=============================

Broadcom ships StorCLI for Linux only as an x86_64 binary.  This package
runs that official binary, unmodified, through a statically linked
qemu-x86_64 user-mode emulator built for the local architecture.

Files
  /opt/MegaRAID/storcli/storcli64             wrapper, same path as upstream
  /opt/MegaRAID/storcli/x86_64/storcli64      official Broadcom binary
  /opt/MegaRAID/storcli/x86_64/qemu-x86_64    static QEMU user-mode emulator

The QEMU build carries a patch (qemu-patches/) that passes the MegaRAID
management ioctl (MEGASAS_IOC_FIRMWARE, MEGASAS_IOC_GET_AEN) and SCSI
generic SG_IO through to the host kernel, translating the guest pointers
embedded in those structures.

LoongArch: only new-world (ABI2.0, kernel >= 5.19) systems are supported.
The wrapper refuses to run on old-world kernels.

